1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,410
Have you ever wondered why your brother or sister doesn’t look exactly like you despite having the same family tree?
你有没有想过，为什么你和兄弟姐妹有着相同的家族谱系，长相却不完全一样？

2
00:00:09,410 --> 00:00:18,960
If you think that’s odd, even stranger is the idea that you and your sibling may have very different ancestry genes.
如果你觉得这件事很奇怪，那更不可思议的是，你和兄弟姐妹可能携带差异很大的祖先基因。

3
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:30,840
You have the same parents, and therefore the exact same ancestors, but somehow your DNA tests come back with very different results.
你们有着相同的父母，自然也有着完全相同的先祖，但DNA检测结果却莫名其妙地大相径庭。

4
00:00:30,840 --> 00:00:33,750
How is this even possible?
这究竟是怎么回事呢？

5
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:42,400
Children inherit half of their DNA from each parent, via the sperm from the father and the egg from the mother.
孩子会从父母双方各继承一半的DNA，分别来自父亲的精子和母亲的卵子。

6
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:48,400
Our bodies contain 46 chromosomes, or 23 pairs.
人体含有46条染色体，也就是23对。

7
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:55,230
However, each reproductive cell has only 23 individual chromosomes.
但每个生殖细胞只含有23条独立的染色体。

8
00:00:55,230 --> 00:01:09,840
When the bodies of our forbearers created their sex cells, the cells engaged in genetic reshuffling, meaning each of the 23 chromosomes is a unique combination of an original pair.
当我们祖先的身体产生生殖细胞时，这些细胞会发生基因重组，也就是说这23条染色体中的每一条，都是其原始染色体对的独特组合。

9
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:14,400
This process is also called genetic recombination.
这个过程也被称为遗传重组。

10
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:33,270
This is why Dr. Prosanta Chakrabarty, a scientist who studies fish to help explain the evolution of human beings and our planet, says that your sister could be 10% more "French" than you, despite having the same primogenitors.
正因如此，通过研究鱼类来解释人类及地球进化历程的科学家普洛桑塔·查克拉巴蒂博士表示，即便拥有相同的直系祖先，你的姐妹也可能比你多10%的“法国血统”。

11
00:01:33,270 --> 00:01:38,260
And the further you go back in your lineage, the more confusing it can be.
而且追溯的谱系年代越久远，情况可能就越复杂。

12
00:01:38,260 --> 00:01:43,800
You inherit 25% of each grandparent's DNA.
你会从每位祖父母那里继承25%的DNA。

13
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:53,440
However, this process of recombination means that inevitably some of their genetic make-up will be lost along the way.
但遗传重组的过程意味着，他们的部分基因构成必然会在遗传过程中丢失。

14
00:01:53,440 --> 00:02:00,940
This could mean that the genes you inherited from your grandparent, could be completely different to those your cousin received.
这就可能导致你从祖父母那里继承的基因，和你的表亲所继承的基因完全不同。

15
00:02:00,940 --> 00:02:14,170
Those studying genealogy should also be aware that modern DNA testing might not give you an accurate idea of your ancestry as it is tested against a current, but incomplete database.
研究家谱学的人还应当注意，现代DNA检测或许无法准确呈现你的先祖谱系，因为检测所参照的数据库虽然是最新的，但并不完整。

16
00:02:14,170 --> 00:02:26,960
Many of the genetic samples come from North America and Western Europe. The genes passed down from your ancestors is sampled and matched with people who originated from a certain area.
许多基因样本都来自北美和西欧，检测时会将你祖先传下来的基因取样，与特定地区起源人群的基因进行比对。

17
00:02:26,960 --> 00:02:34,810
However, without enough samples from the Middle East or Africa, the results may be inaccurate.
但由于缺乏来自中东或非洲的足够样本，检测结果可能存在偏差。

18
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:45,960
Dr. Prosanta Chakrabarty says that only 1% of our genetic make-up is unique to us, and that it is an incomplete mash-up of our ancestors’.
普洛桑塔·查克拉巴蒂博士称，我们的基因构成中只有1%是独属于自己的，其余都是祖先基因的不完全混合体。

19
00:02:45,960 --> 00:02:54,840
So, the next time someone says you look a bit like you're from a certain country, you may well be. But it might not show up in your tests.
所以下次再有人说你看起来像某个国家的人时，这种感觉很可能是对的，但这一点或许不会在你的DNA检测结果中体现出来。
